      <resourceMetadata>
        <identifier>HydroBASINS South America, Level 8, Version 1.c - Sub-basins in standard format (without lakes)</identifier>
        <parentidentifier></parentidentifier>
        <language></language>
        <type>dataset</type>
        <title>HydroBASINS South America, Level 8, Version 1.c - Sub-basins in standard format (without lakes)</title>
        <abstract>All HydroBASINS layers were derived from World Wildlife Fund’s HydroSHEDS data based on a grid resolution of 15 arc-seconds (approximately 500 m at the equator). Watersheds were delineated in a consistent manner at different scales, and a hierarchical sub-basin breakdown was created following the topological concept of the Pfafstetter coding system. The resulting polygon layers are termed HydroBASINS and represent a subset of the HydroSHEDS database. This shapefile contains (sub-)basin polygons for South America at Pfafstetter level 8.

HydroBASINS data provides a series of polygon layers that depict watershed boundaries and sub-basin delineations at a global scale. The goal of this product is to provide a seamless global coverage of consistently sized and hierarchically nested sub-basins at different scales (from tens to millions of square kilometers), supported by a coding scheme that allows for analysis of watershed topology such as up- and downstream connectivity.</abstract>
        <keywords vocabulary="Search keys">
          <keyword>HydroBASINS</keyword>
          <keyword>HydrSHEDS</keyword>
        </keywords>
        <contact>
          <name></name>
          <organization></organization>
          <position></position>
          <voice></voice>
          <fax></fax>
